==English==
[[Image:The Levant 3.png|thumb|the '''Levant''']]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|levant||[[rising]], sun's point of rising}}, form of {{m|fr|lever||to rise}}, from {{der|en|la|levō||to rise}} (cf. also the present participle {{m|la|levāns}}), from {{m|la|levis||light, not heavy}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈlɛv.ənt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ləˈvɑnt/|/lɛvɑnt/|/ləˈvænt/|a=GenAm}}
* {{rhymes|en|ænt|s=2}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{sid|en|Q81483}}{{place|en|cultural region|r/Western Asia|consisting of the countries bordering the eastern [[Mediterranean Sea]], namely [[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Palestine]], [[Jordan]] and [[Cyprus]] (and sometimes, especially in a historical context, also including [[Turkey]] and [[Egypt]], then part of the [[Ottoman Empire]])|tcl=a <<cultural region>> of <<r/Western Asia>> consisting of the eastern [[Mediterranean]] countries, i.e. [[Syria]], [[Lebanon]], [[Israel]], [[Palestine]], [[Jordan]] and [[Cyprus]]}}.
#: {{syn|en|Mashreq|Greater Syria}}

